":"1785955304653007001-f833e4e0-008d-4aa7-88e4-1dcb3d9307d6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7b6d1c4313709b72ab541ccf0e996eac91ce2afbd2b6e834dac49c8f29814dc3","event_uuid":"019a8f69-f5cf-4a92-8055-d1de6c236703","position":{"commit_sha":"8534125048500d947f45182deba78f05a148004c","position":"1785957475434230001-019a8f69-f5cf-4a92-8055-d1de6c236703"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ddd95c9b6d9ff4e74af7ff14e30cc33ae57783fd73c17f55f15ec5791a6b9f5e","event_uuid":"e78d46a3-df7d-4ea2-9b87-1abeed0b849e","position":{"commit_sha":"aa824b4433ef090e6f758fdfa8860520b5180cbc","position":"1785959297615103001-e78d46a3-df7d-4ea2-9b87-1abeed0b849e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Blocking-review remediation completed without production-code edits. The isolated feature worktree was fast-forwarded to current origin/main 0f5dbc88b before remeasurement. Ruff 0.15.19 now reports 53 C901 diagnostics (not the prior 52) and a maximum score of 45; the exact command is: ruff check --select C901 --config 'lint.mccabe.max-complexity=15' --exit-zero --statistics src/rebar. Observed output: \"53 C901 complex-structure\" and \"Found 53 errors.\" The plan now specifies the complete JSON object schema, normalized path::AST-qualified-symbol key grammar, integer ceiling constraints, duplicate/unknown/malformed rejection, and mutually exclusive active/new/increased/stale counters with exact exit behavior. check-ac, clarity-check 5/5, and quality-check all pass. Because the plan and base SHA changed, a fresh signed review is required; prior remediation eligibility is not reused.","timestamp":1784506926869261001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Remediated the remaining G6 exit-code ambiguity. Empirical current-base probe confirms raw_rc=1 raw_count=53 and census_rc=0 census_count=53 when the only difference is Ruff's explicit --exit-zero option. The plan now separates: (1) raw Ruff, which exits 1 because 53 over-threshold functions exist; (2) machine-readable Ruff census with --exit-zero, which exits 0 solely so JSON can be consumed; and (3) the repository wrapper, which independently exits 0 only when all current findings are at/below recorded ceilings and no scanner/schema error exists. Approach, tests, help contract, and separate ACs now pin all three behaviors. check-ac passes with 15 items, quality-check passes, and clarity-check scores 5/5. Fresh signed review required.","timestamp":1784509659994694001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Review remediation from the latest signed-review candidate: added guarded --update-stale maintenance mode that can only lower/remove debt and refuses new/increased findings; made the production-only complexity scope versus existing src/tests lint scope explicit; aligned the maintenance runbook contract with threshold 15 and src/rebar; and specified AST identity behavior/tests for nested functions, lambdas, overloads, and duplicate qualified keys. No production code was changed.","timestamp":1784517664978344001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Remediated the two latest G6 blockers. The scanner command is now stated exactly as [\n  {\n    \"cell\": null,\n    \"code\": \"C901\",\n    \"end_location\": {\n      \"column\": 14,\n      \"row\": 189\n    },\n    \"filename\": \"/private/tmp/rebar-quality-ratchet/src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py\",\n    \"fix\": null,\n    \"location\": {\n      \"column\": 5,\n      \"row\": 189\n    },\n    \"message\": \"`_dispatch` is too complex (36 > 10)\",\n    \"noqa_row\": 189,\n    \"url\": \"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/complex-structure\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"cell\": null,\n    \"code\": \"C901\",\n    \"end_location\": {\n      \"column\": 19,\n      \"row\": 368\n    },\n    \"filename\": \"/private/tmp/rebar-quality-ratchet/src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py\",\n    \"fix\": null,\n    \"location\": {\n      \"column\": 5,\n      \"row\": 368\n    },\n    \"message\": \"`_main_dispatch` is too complex (35 > 10)\",\n    \"noqa_row\": 368,\n    \"url\": \"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/complex-structure\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"cell\": null,\n    \"code\": \"C901\",\n    \"end_location\": {\n      \"column\": 14,\n      \"row\": 31\n    },\n    \"filename\": \"/private/tmp/rebar-quality-ratchet/src/rebar/_cli/_audit_commands.py\",\n    \"fix\": null,\n    \"location\": {\n      \"column\": 5,\n      \"row\": 31\n    },\n    \"message\": \"`audit_cli` is too complex (14 > 10)\",\n    \"noqa_row\": 31,\n    \"url\": \"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/complex-structure\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"cell\": null,\n    \"code\": \"C901\",\n    \"end_location\": {\n      \"column\": 17,\n      \"row\": 97\n    },\n    \"filename\": \"/private/tmp/rebar-quality-ratchet/src/rebar/_cli/_audit_commands.py\"