mplex-structure\"\n  }\n] for both modes. The wrapper accepts return codes 0 and 1 as diagnostic-bearing operation only after validating C901 JSON; return code 2+ remains a scanner failure.  now reuses  instead of a bespoke temp/replace sequence, with tests requiring unchanged target bytes and no leftover sibling temp after injected write or replace failures. No production code was changed.","timestamp":1784523245781312001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Corrected remediation record (supersedes the malformed preceding comment): the scanner command is exactly `ruff check --select C901 --exit-zero --output-format=json src/rebar` for both modes. Return codes 0 and 1 proceed only after valid C901 JSON is confirmed; return code 2 or greater is a scanner failure. The update-stale path reuses `rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write`, with tests requiring unchanged target bytes and no leftover sibling temp file after injected write or replace failures. No production code was changed.","timestamp":1784523332207682001},{"author":"reconciler","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Remediated the two latest G6 blockers. The scanner command is now stated exactly as [\n  {\n    \"cell\": null,\n    \"code\": \"C901\",\n    \"end_location\": {\n      \"column\": 14,\n      \"row\": 189\n    },\n    \"filename\": \"/private/tmp/rebar-quality-ratchet/src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py\",\n    \"fix\": null,\n    \"location\": {\n      \"column\": 5,\n      \"row\": 189\n    },\n    \"message\": \"`_dispatch` is too complex (36 > 10)\",\n    \"noqa_row\": 189,\n    \"url\": \"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/complex-structure\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"cell\": null,\n    \"code\": \"C901\",\n    \"end_location\": {\n      \"column\": 19,\n      \"row\": 368\n    },\n    \"filename\": \"/private/tmp/rebar-quality-ratchet/src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py\",\n    \"fix\": null,\n    \"loc